From b29340392d893084a9e38e9c1a73b8d785da5d1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 10:04:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/51] begonia-wifi (fwport-pmic): port A-die LDO LP + flag
 absent EMI-MPU API

The conn A-die PMIC path was stubbed at the API level (no-op
KERNEL_pmic_ldo_vcn*_lp / KERNEL_pmic_set_register_value bodies in
mtk-bsp-compat). Port them to REAL mt6359 PMIC regmap ops in mt6785.c,
following the f9650bf5a clock-buffer pattern, so consys_hw_vcn18_ctrl /
consys_hw_vcn28_ctrl actually take the conn A-die rails out of low-power
and tie them to SRCLKEN0 hardware-LP control:

  - wmt_pmic_ldo_lp(): faithful port of vendor pmic_ldo_vcn*_lp()
    (pmic_lp_type_set semantics) - SW user maps to OP_EN[15] SW operator;
    SRCLKEN0 user maps to CON0 OP_MODE select + OP_EN/OP_CFG bit0.
  - wmt_pmic_set_ldo_lp(): faithful port of
    KERNEL_pmic_set_register_value(PMIC_RG_LDO_VCN*_LP, 0): clear CON0[1].

mt6359 offsets (PMIC_REG_BASE==0): VCN18 CON0 0x1c2a/OP_EN 0x1c2e/OP_CFG
0x1c34; VCN33_2 CON0 0x1c08/OP_EN 0x1c0c/OP_CFG 0x1c12; LP bit[1];
OP_MODE[12:10]; SRCLKEN0 op = bit0; SW op = bit15.

3-source bar met for every register op:
  (1) vendor intent: the KERNEL_pmic_ldo_*_lp / KERNEL_pmic_set_register_value
      call sites in mt6785.c.
  (2) proven reimpl op: mtk-conninfra-mt6785.c
      (mtk_conninfra_ldo_sw_op_en / mtk_conninfra_ldo_hw_mode), reaches
      conn idle 0x1d1e on hardware.
  (3) field def: include/linux/mfd/mt6359/registers.h + mt6785 upmu_hw.h
      (begonia-r-oss) + pmic_lp_api.c selector model (SRCLKEN0=0, SW=15).

EMI-MPU (consys_emi_mpu_set_region_protection): FLAGGED, NOT PORTED.
Mainline 6.16 has no MTK EMI driver (drivers/memory/mediatek ships only
mtk-smi.o; no mtk-emi.c, no mtk_emimpu_* symbol) and CONFIG_MTK_EMI is
unset, so the vendor emi_mpu_set_protection() body never compiled. This is
an access-protection table, NOT the conn firmware-fetch path (that is the
0xF0000000 EMI-window remap, which the reimpl proves works without any MPU
call). Replaced the silent ifdef no-op with an explicit logged skip + flag
comment; documented likewise in the mt_emi_api.h compat stub.

Also: drop a dead include of linux/regmap.h that f9650bf5a left inside the
copyright comment block; add a real include in the header section.

bsp-compat: the pmic_set/get_register_value no-op bodies are now dead on
the begonia path (call sites bypass the KERNEL_* macro); kept only for any
non-begonia caller and re-commented. No-ops intentionally LEFT (off the
begonia BTIF bring-up path): mt6306 GPIO expander, SDIO CMD52, show_stack /
dump_thread_state debug, platform_bridge / SDIO eirq.

Build: pmbootstrap build --src OK; wmt_pmic_ldo_lp + EMI-skip string
verified present in wmt_drv.ko.

Signed-off-by: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
